From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matteo Geromin <geromin.matteo@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:01:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: configs: bbb_printer: disable the software watchdog

softdog was built in and registered before omap_wdt, so it became
/dev/watchdog0 and systemd used it as "hardware" watchdog. softdog does
not reset the board when the kernel itself hangs. Disable it, so the
OMAP hardware watchdog is /dev/watchdog0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/bbb_printer_defconfig b/arch/arm/configs/bbb_printer_defconfig
index 70f8bff..44f7c7b 100644
--- a/arch/arm/configs/bbb_printer_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/bbb_printer_defconfig
@@ -1362,7 +1362,7 @@ CONFIG_WATCHDOG_SYSFS=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG_PRETIMEOUT_GOV=y
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG_PRETIMEOUT_GOV_PANIC=m
 CONFIG_WATCHDOG_PRETIMEOUT_DEFAULT_GOV_NOOP=y
-CONFIG_SOFT_WATCHDOG=y
+# CONFIG_SOFT_WATCHDOG is not set
 CONFIG_OMAP_WATCHDOG=y
 CONFIG_MFD_STMPE=y
 CONFIG_MFD_TI_AM335X_TSCADC=y
